Local workaround: load vision weights for NemotronH_Omni_Reasoning_V3 exports.

vLLM's nano_nemotron_vl load_weights() routes tensors through four prefix
predicates in an if/elif chain with no else branch. This checkpoint names the
tower `vision_model.encoder.layer.N.*` / `vision_model.embeddings.*` and the
projector `vision_projector.*`, which match none of them, so 586 tensors are
dropped silently and the vision tower runs on random init. The model then
returns fluent but fabricated image descriptions instead of failing.

Purely additive: a separate bucket plus a mapper. Checkpoints that use the
upstream `vision_model.radio_model.*` / `mlp1` layout are unaffected.

Not upstreamed: the checkpoint stores separate Q/K/V where vLLM expects a
packed attn.qkv, and ships vision_projector.vision_final_layernorm.* for which
mlp1 has no slot, so the correct long-term fix may be a checkpoint re-export.
Tracking nvbug to be filed; see PR discussion.

